    <string name="accessibility_label">Voicemator dictation</string>
    <string name="accessibility_summary">Floating button to dictate, and text typed straight into the field you are editing.</string>
    <string name="accessibility_description">Adds a floating accessibility button that starts and stops dictation, and pastes the transcription into the text field you are editing. To find that field, Voicemator looks at the screen only at the moment it inserts text. Speech is transcribed on this device; nothing is sent anywhere or stored outside the app.</string>
    <string name="setup_accessibility_title">Floating button and typing into fields (optional)</string>
    <string name="setup_accessibility_body">Turn on Voicemator in Accessibility settings and choose the floating accessibility button as its shortcut. Tap the button to dictate; the text goes straight into the field you are editing. Android will warn that the app can see the screen: Voicemator only uses this to find the focused field when inserting text.</string>
